@startuml
title SIC/XE Macro Processor - Modes of the One-Pass Algorithm

skinparam shadowing false

state "Normal\n\nd = 0, e = false\na source line is copied or is a call" as Normal
state "Definition\n\nd > 0\nthe line is stored in the current definition" as Definition
state "Expansion\n\nd = 0, e = true\nlines come from the top frame" as Expansion
state "Stopped\n\na limit was reached\nstopped = true, no line is read" as Stopped

[*] --> Normal

Normal --> Normal : other line / copy to MASMAPRG.ASM
Normal --> Definition : MCDEFN / d + 1
Normal --> Expansion : call / push frame, serial + 1
Normal --> Stopped : call over a limit

Definition --> Definition : MCDEFN / d + 1
Definition --> Definition : MCEND with d > 1 / d - 1
Definition --> Definition : other line, calls included / store
Definition --> Normal : MCEND with d = 1, stack empty /\nd - 1, close definition
Definition --> Expansion : MCEND with d = 1, stack not empty /\nd - 1, close definition
Definition --> Stopped : limit reached while expanding

Expansion --> Expansion : body line / copy to MASMAPRG.ASM
Expansion --> Expansion : nested call / push frame, serial + 1
Expansion --> Expansion : body MCEND, stack not empty / pop frame
Expansion --> Normal : body MCEND, stack empty / pop frame
Expansion --> Definition : MCDEFN read from the body / d + 1
Expansion --> Stopped : limit reached

Normal --> [*] : end of text
Definition --> [*] : end of text /\nMCDEFN without MCEND
Stopped --> [*]

note right of Definition
A definition can open while expanding:
the stack keeps its frames, so e stays true,
and closing it returns to Expansion.
end note

note right of Stopped
stop(): the error goes to the outermost call,
open expansions end, the stack is cleared.
Other errors are reported and processing
goes on in the same mode.
end note

note bottom of Normal
Trace view pill (MacroTrace.tsx, modeOf):
Definition when d > 0 or the step is define-start,
else Expansion when e, else Normal.
end note

@enduml
